  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 13.14 (page number not visible in the photos). Book: EFL 101.4, BFL 17.04, NA -0.4929 (F/1.01), GIH 27.16 (HFOV=15.00), PTZ/F -0.8344, VL 161.8, infinite conjugate. Glass: BSC1 entered as model glass 1.511,63.5 (no dispersion data found); C2 entered as model glass 1.513,60.5 (no dispersion data found); EDF2 entered as model glass 1.689,30.9 (no dispersion data found). The book does not mark the stop; it is placed at surface 7, the front of the rear group, after the long air space (the table has no plane stop row; the smallest semi-apertures belong to the rear group or field flattener near the image). The book designs this lens for a curved image surface, but its table gives no image radius, so the image here is plane. Entered exactly as printed, the table gives EFL 104.0 instead of the book's 101.4: the last surface reads as plane (blank radius), and a radius near -340 there would reproduce the book's EFL and BFL, so a radius may be missing from the printed table.",
